[[0,1322004,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-03T00:51:50","youareivan","",[],"<p>so kevin hart...</p>\n<p>am i missing something? i have seen him occasionally on conan and he's o.k. there. i've also seen some of his stand up on comedy central and found it to be utterly forgettable. the only thing i've seen from his acting work are clips and i wasn't very interested in his shenanigans.</p>\n<p>is his popularity a result of there not being many mainstream comedians who aren't identity politics influenced moral scolds that might show how unimpressive his comedy stylings are by comparison, or is there some of his work that anyone could point me to that represents his good stuff.</p>","am i missing something?","","comedy"],[1,6469548,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-03T02:28:53","Sosacms","",[],"<p>He's popular because enough people like his comedy style and acting. I strongly disagree, but that's generally how popularity works. Generic enough to pull in more people. The pop music of comedy. </p>"]]
