[[0,1322019,0,46,1,45,"2016-10-03T00:57:42","TrumptoMaga","",[],"<p>Is there a way to get the word out to the rest of the unaware subs there? It is clearly infiltrated by censoring mods/admins or shills for Hitlery.</p>","As a original subscriber of /r/the_donald, with over 100k link karma, I have officially been shadowbanned, I think.","","TheDonald"],[1,6468950,0,3,0,3,"2016-10-03T01:05:17","KosherHiveKicker","[e]",[],"<p>Test it here.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"http://nullprogram.com/am-i-shadowbanned/\">http://nullprogram.com/am-i-shadowbanned/</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>-or here-</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/ShadowBan/\">https://www.reddit.com/r/ShadowBan/</a></li>\n</ul>"],[2,6468962,6468950,3,0,3,"2016-10-03T01:06:57","TrumptoMaga","",[],"<p>Not shadowbanned on reddit overall. just on the_donald apparently. Its def one of the mods who did it and not sitewide</p>"],[3,6468989,6468962,0,0,0,"2016-10-03T01:10:48","KosherHiveKicker","",[],"<p>Hmmm.</p>\n<p>Try posting in the comment section of someone else's thread.... then log out and return to the page. \r</p>\n<p>IF you are shadowbanned in that subreddit, THEN it might disappear.</p>"],[4,6469510,6468989,0,0,0,"2016-10-03T02:22:03","TrumptoMaga","",[],"<p>You know what I think it is? I can reply to comments on there but new posts must be picked up by the spam filter or something. They are legitimate posts as well.</p>"],[1,6469629,0,7,0,7,"2016-10-03T02:41:38","ex-redd","",[],"<p>jump ship and never mention it again...lost cause hommie</p>"],[1,6469836,0,3,0,3,"2016-10-03T03:21:28","Slayfire122","",[],"<p>Try looking at your comments when you're not logged in. </p>"],[1,6469884,0,2,0,2,"2016-10-03T03:28:53","BentAxel","",[],"<p>If its worth anything, no one gives a fuck about the political users on Reddit. They are fucking imbeciles. </p>"],[1,6469985,0,0,0,0,"2016-10-03T03:46:46","ThisIsntMe123","",[],"<p>Can you do the getting a bunch of IP's banned? Like coffee shops and alike?</p>"],[1,6470267,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-03T04:37:36","guinness2","[e]",[],"<p>Come and join us and enjoy the freedom to express yourself honestly.</p>\n<p>Voat tends to have far smaller communities that Reddit, but that's not a bad thing because the quality tends to be better because we can speak honestly and sincerely.</p>\n<p>That said, there is a yuge number of conservative, nationalistic, anti-globalism, right-wing supporters here, but that's not our fault... it's because leftists don't tend to last long away from their safe spaces. Once they've rebutted your argument by calling you a racist and after you ask &quot;what's wrong with racism if it's based on informed and rational reason?&quot;, they have nowhere else to go, but to crawl back under the rock from which they came.</p>\n<p>I wish there were more leftists here, but they either run away or become spammers who aren't interested in formal debate and are just here to preach at us without the risk of considering opposing opinions.</p>"],[1,6470510,0,0,0,0,"2016-10-03T05:34:16","PM_ME_UR_NOODZ","",[],"<p>Where do you draw the line between original subscriber and unoriginal subsrciber?</p>"],[1,6471518,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-03T10:35:54","the_magic_man","",[],"<p>The_Donald is one of the most heavily censored subs on reddit. No surprise you were eventually banned for some reason </p>"],[1,6503589,0,0,0,0,"2016-10-07T03:57:29","Sgt_richard","",[],"<p>Fuck reddit. They just temp banned me for calling them out on their censorship. The mods in the_Donald have been compromised. They promote bullshit 'my vaginas hurts' stories and bury the important ones. I'm not going back. They can burn for all I care. </p>"]]
[[1,6469623,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-03T02:40:39","TheScattMan","",[],"<p>On one hand, I hate the principle of State funded television, especially in the case of modern PBS because it is essentially CNN-lite, but then agian I'm reminded about the quality of its past programs when compared to the garbage that's been on TV for last 20 years.</p>\n<p>IDK, I just want to live my life and stop caring about this shit, so start by not forcing me to pay for it out of my taxes.</p>"],[2,6471966,6469623,0,0,0,"2016-10-03T13:07:18","nuworldblue","",[],"<p>How should it be payed for? Its not like Cartoon Network is gonna start airing quality educational content. This isn't the kind of programming that makes crazy ad revenue rain on television producers. The reason that Public Broadcasting has been quality in the past is that it is non-profit and payed for by taxpayers. It is a good service that we <em>should</em> value and protect. </p>"],[3,6556882,6471966,0,0,0,"2016-10-13T21:21:46","TheScattMan","",[],"<p>You make a good point, but this same type of arguement can be used to defend any government institution, and we find ourselves at a cross roads, where are government is too big and powerful, but we don't want to cut anything. In that regard, it's hard to justify, as a public broadcast of any kind (PBS, NPR, etc) is not related to national defense, or upholding rights, etc. If anything it is education, and as such It should be funded only at the State level. If Oregon wants PBS, go for it. If Texas doesn't, don't make them pay the taxes.</p>\n<p>I'm making more of a philosophical point, and actually don't know exactly how PBS is funded. It may very well be a state by state thing, and if thats the case, then I fully support it. </p>"]]
